meta {
  name: 01 Start Login
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/login
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Starts the real OpenEMR authorization_code login flow. Expect: 307,
  Location header pointing at https://<openemr-host>/oauth2/default/authorize
  with this app's real client_id/redirect_uri/scope/state/PKCE challenge --
  confirmed live 2026-09-20.

  Depending on your Bruno client's redirect-following setting, you may see
  this raw 307 (Location header visible) or the followed OpenEMR sign-in
  page HTML instead. Either is fine for confirming the redirect fires; this
  request cannot complete the interactive sign-in + consent screens that
  follow, since that needs a real browser -- see bruno/README.md for how to
  actually obtain a working session from this flow.

  This is NOT itself a /chat auth check -- it only proves /login redirects
  correctly. Use auth/03 Me to confirm whether your copilot_session
  environment variable is currently valid.
}
